        <a href={TEL} class="brx-btn">Call {PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OLDER HOMES -->
  <section class="brx-sec" id="older-homes">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What if you live in an older Liverpool house?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Many Liverpool homes are Victorian, Edwardian or 1930s, and their heating has often been changed several times. That is fine, but it needs checking first.</p>
      <ul class="brx-list">
        <li><strong>Back boilers</strong> behind a gas fire are still found in older terraces. They are taken out and replaced with a wall-mounted boiler, and the fireplace is made good or capped.</li>
        <li><strong>Gravity-fed systems</strong> with tanks in the loft can be kept with a new regular boiler, or converted to a combi or system boiler if the water pressure allows.</li>
        <li><strong>Old pipework and radiators</strong> often hold years of sludge. They are cleaned before the new boiler goes on, or <a href="/power-flushing-liverpool">power flushed</a> if they are badly blocked.</li>
        <li><strong>Condensate pipes</strong> that run outside can freeze in a cold snap and stop the boiler. We route and insulate them to reduce the risk.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- RULES -->
  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="rules">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What are the rules for fitting a new boiler?</h2>
      <div class="brx-two">
        <div>
          <h3>Gas Safe registration</h3>
          <p>By law, gas boilers must be fitted by a Gas Safe registered engineer. You can check any engineer on the <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gas Safe Register</a> website.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Controls</h3>
          <p>New boilers in England must be fitted with time and temperature controls. Combi boilers also need an extra energy-saving feature, such as a smart thermostat with automation and optimisation. That is included in our price.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Notifying Building Control</h3>
          <p>A new boiler has to be notified to Building Control. We do that through Gas Safe Register, and you get the certificate by post.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Gas boilers are still allowed</h3>
          <p>You can replace a gas boiler in an existing home with a new gas boiler. The rules that limit gas boilers apply to newly built homes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
